nd $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380595 1113 #uuid "2af6f312-d668-5544-bc66-0a068fde3eb8" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380595 1145 "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=8,$ and since $B$ is formed by $5$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 5+\\text{nullity}(A) & =8 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =8-5 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380597 13194139536041 true] [17592186380596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380598 13194139536041 true] [17592186380596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380599 13194139536041 true] [17592186380596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380600 13194139536041 true] [17592186380596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380601 13194139536041 true] [17592186380596 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536041 true] [17592186380596 1041 "selection" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380596 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380597 13194139536041 true] [17592186380596 1110 #uuid "e023e1c0-dafe-520f-9db8-1da79e499e1e" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380597 1034 "3" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536041 true] [17592186380597 1111 #uuid "8465f0fc-cb7c-5d6b-bcb3-e57968cc582f" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380598 1034 "2" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536041 true] [17592186380598 1111 #uuid "7c63647f-3f27-5317-b3c7-9ee5cee9eace" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380599 1034 "6" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536041 true] [17592186380599 1111 #uuid "1a50727b-68d5-516b-813c-30147d4e7f27" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380600 1034 "4" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536041 true] [17592186380600 1111 #uuid "9c964c65-f97c-5abd-94f0-bf9bf59d7c14" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380601 1034 "5" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380601 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536041 true] [17592186380601 1111 #uuid "5b170c5c-6151-589b-a493-43d082a73ed4" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380602 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380603 13194139536041 true] [17592186380602 1089 "q-142544" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380602 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536041 true] [17592186380602 1100 "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix which has only $3$ non-pivot column?\n\n- $A$ is  **not** invertible\n- $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$\n- $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380602 1113 #uuid "6011c5e7-8c57-59d8-856d-f61a86c3b068" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380602 1145 "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=7=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ has $n=7$ columns and $3$ of them is a non-pivot one, it follows that    \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Col}(A))=7-3=4\\ne 7.\n$$\n\n Thus,  according to the invertible matrix theorem $A$ is  **not** an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true.  Indeed, since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=\\text{rank}(A)=4$,  then $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $n=7$, according to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =7 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =7-4 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139536041 true] [1