+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ has $n=5$ columns and $1$ of them is a non-pivot one, it follows that    \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5-1=4\\ne 5.\n$$\n\n Thus, according to the invertible matrix theorem $A$ is  **not** an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=\\text{rank}(A)=4$,  then $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $n=5$, according to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380638 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380639 13194139536041 true] [17592186380638 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380640 13194139536041 true] [17592186380638 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380641 13194139536041 true] [17592186380638 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380642 13194139536041 true] [17592186380638 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380643 13194139536041 true] [17592186380638 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536041 true] [17592186380638 1041 "selection" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380638 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380640 13194139536041 true] [17592186380638 1110 #uuid "ad7daef0-2c15-5e93-99b2-4a439fa1efed" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380639 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536041 true] [17592186380639 1111 #uuid "f738c2fe-b2a7-5fab-bc25-4d0425020ac5" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380640 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536041 true] [17592186380640 1111 #uuid "738cba16-c53f-5666-8bc3-b10b76db3013" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380641 1034 "I only" 13194139536041 true] [17592186380641 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536041 true] [17592186380641 1111 #uuid "9b8d88f5-0880-5586-99